Package: dmrfit
Date: 2026-10-06
Type: Package
Title: Optimization Tools for Discrete Markov Random Fields
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(person(given = "Giuseppe",
             family = "Arena",
             role = c("aut", "cre"),
             email = "g.arena@uva.nl",
             comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5204-3326")))
Description: Estimation of discrete Markov Random Fields through the pseudolikelihood, for both Ising models (Ising, 1925, <doi:10.1007/BF02980577>) and Ordinal Markov Random Fields (Marsman, M., van den Bergh, D., and Haslbeck, J. M. B, 2025, <doi:10.1017/psy.2024.4>). Point estimates, either maximum pseudolikelihood or maximum a posteriori, are obtained through a trust region optimization algorithm, with robust standard errors from the Huber-White sandwich estimator, for both full and constrained network structures. Bayesian inference corrects the pseudo-posterior through coordinate rescaling, which matches its covariance to the sandwich covariance, and samples from it with an adaptive Fisher-preconditioned Metropolis-adjusted Langevin algorithm. Savage-Dickey Bayes factors test each pairwise interaction, computed either by sampling importance resampling or from the posterior draws.
